# 2. Chatwoot is not our core CRM

The original call describes Chatwoot essentially as:

> everything gets centralized there, therefore it is the CRM.

That's only partly correct. 

Chatwoot is excellent as the **conversation/inbox layer**:

```text
WhatsApp ─────┐
Instagram ────┼──► Chatwoot
Facebook ─────┘
                  │
                  ├── conversations
                  ├── agents
                  ├── assignments
                  ├── labels
                  └── human handoff
```

It currently supports multiple inboxes/channels, including WhatsApp and Instagram, and its WhatsApp integration is built around the official Cloud API. ([Chatwoot][2])

But I would **not make Chatwoot the authoritative source for the business state**.

Instead:

```text
Chatwoot
System of Engagement

        │

PostgreSQL
System of Record
```

PostgreSQL should own things such as:

```text
lead
customer
student
order
payment
lead_stage
lead_score
engagement
followup
subscription
AI execution
```

Chatwoot owns:

```text
conversation
inbox
agent
human assignment
message presentation
```

That separation is much cleaner.

